.TH CLEAR 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
clear \- clear the terminal screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clear
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clear
moves the cursor home, erases the screen, and erases the terminal's
scrollback, by writing the escape sequences
.B ESC[H ESC[2J ESC[3J
to standard output, as ncurses'
.B clear
does.
Any arguments are ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stty (1)
